<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kushano-Sasanian Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 230–365 CE</span> · Also known as Kushanshahs, Indo-Sasanians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kushano-Sasanian Kingdom was the realm of Sasanian princes who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> and parts of Gandhara after the Sasanian conquest of the western Kushan lands in the 3rd century CE. Its rulers styled themselves Kushanshah, &quot;king of the Kushans&quot;, and issued coins that blended Kushan and Sasanian designs. It gave way in the later 4th century to the Kidarites.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kushano-sasanian-kingdom.jpg" alt="Kushano-Sasanian Kingdom" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HistoryofIran · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Kushano-Sasanian_Kingdom.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
